From d676e23bfe8d581bb517593f10ef9814a0c7fbdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:40:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 131/159] domainset: the trie a type of its own, filled in
 place

domain.ReadMatcher copies the trie it is handed, growing its slices a
chunk at a time, while the trie it reads is still held: for a rule set
of a million names that copy was the peak of the load.

common/domainset/succinct is the succinct set of sing as a type of its
own, with sing's code to match it and to index it (common/domain,
after openacid/succinct) copied without a change. The builder fills it
in place; a big trie is cut down to what it holds, after the garbage of
the build is collected. Rules read by ReadSource carry it as DomainSet
(json:"-"), and route/rule makes a domain item of it. The matcher of
sing stays for binary rule sets.

The item of a set tells of itself what route/rule told of a domain item
of the lists (domainset.Describe, which NewDomainItem uses too). An empty
name in domain or domain_suffix is left to route/rule, which refuses it:
the reader built it before.

TestSetMatchesAsSing holds Match to sing's on the names of random lists,
their subdomains, the names a suffix is cut from, capitals, names not of
ASCII and words; the bytes of a set are sing's.

A rule set of a million names (21 MB of JSON), x86, GOMAXPROCS=4: the
peak RSS of ReadSource +92 MB before, +40-46 MB now; 300000 names +13 MB.
